ADR-0023 revises ADR-0011, which stays accepted: its criterion did not change,
only the number of operations that meet it. Five SQL functions became eight. It
also records why `security invoker` was written first and had to be abandoned —
the `app` schema is revoked from `authenticated`, and policies only reach it
because policy expressions run as the table owner.

D-16 (scope has no origin; team comes from memberships, without job titles),
D-17 (yes, transactional boundaries), D-18 (draft never reaches the client) and
D-19 (zero projects is an empty state, never a 404) are settled in
spec-review.md with the reasoning, not just the verdict.

The imperative rules now carry the two obligations this phase creates: an RPC
function lives in `public` and is `definer` for a reason that must be understood
before writing the ninth one, and portal route authorization belongs in the
group layout.

FASE6ESTADO.md records what was validated, what was not, and why — including the
staging ledger drift, the `funcoes` fingerprint divergence that the
comment-stripped first apply caused, and the manual QA checklist that a person
still has to run, because no PostgREST path could be exercised from this session.

